IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `poa-dates`
IMPORT `poa-core`

-- Powers of Attorney Act 1998 (Qld) -- claims about an attorney's dealings, from the seat of the claimant.
--
-- SEAT: the claimant: the principal whose attorney dealt with their affairs (or someone acting for them), or, after the
-- principal's death, the principal's personal representative, a beneficiary of the principal's estate, or a person whose
-- benefit in the estate was lost. "Could my attorney act then? Can the power of attorney be set aside? Was my attorney
-- allowed to do this? Is undue influence presumed? Can I get compensation or the attorney's profits, and by when must I
-- apply? I lost a gift in the will because the attorney sold it: do I take the proceeds, or can I be compensated? Who may
-- apply, to which court, and who pays the costs?" Every question is asked as the claimant would ask it, on facts they
-- can state; the court's and the tribunal's judgments are facts they answer conditionally. The principal is "you" where
-- the principal is asking; a claimant asking after the principal's death answers the same facts about the principal.
-- The rules are in poa-core.l4; this module builds their inputs from plain answers and restates no rule.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Powers of Attorney Act 1998 (Qld) -- the claimant's questions`

DECLARE `Offence answer` IS ONE OF
    `an offence; the most the court can impose is, in penalty units` HAS `penalty units` IS A NUMBER
    `the Act does not settle this: ss 26, 61, 66, 71, 74A and 86 do not make that conduct an offence`

§§ `Was the power exercisable, and was it valid (ss 33, 41, 96-99, 113-114)`

@export Could my attorney under my enduring power of attorney exercise the power for this matter at the time they acted?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Kind of matter` @desc Whether the attorney acted on a financial matter (money, property, bills, a legal matter about money or property) or a personal matter (where you live, your care, your health)
      `my enduring power of attorney says when the power begins` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your enduring power of attorney specifies a time, circumstance or occasion when power for financial matters becomes exercisable
      `that time had come` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that specified time, circumstance or occasion had come when the attorney acted (answer no if none was specified)
      `I could understand decisions about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time, you were capable of understanding the nature and effect of decisions about the matter
      `I could make decisions freely and voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time, you were capable of freely and voluntarily making decisions about the matter
      `I could communicate my decisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time, you were capable of communicating your decisions in some way
GIVETH AN `Exercisable answer`
DECIDE `Could my attorney exercise the power at the time` IS
    `the s 33 answer` `the matter` `my enduring power of attorney says when the power begins` `that time had come`
        (NOT (`has capacity for the matter` `I could understand decisions about the matter` `I could make decisions freely and voluntarily` `I could communicate my decisions`))

@export Can the court (or QCAT, for an enduring document) declare my power of attorney invalid?
GIVEN `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document: a general power of attorney made under the Act; an enduring power of attorney; an advance health directive; a power of attorney made under another law; or a statutory health attorney
      `I made it freely and voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an enduring power of attorney: whether, when you made it, you were capable of making it freely and voluntarily
      `I understood its nature and effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an enduring power of attorney: whether you understood its nature and effect, including that you could limit the power, when it begins, that the attorney would have full control, that you could revoke it while able, that it continues if you lose capacity, and that you could not oversee it once unable to revoke it (s 41(2))
      `I had the capacity needed to make another document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For any other document: whether you had the capacity the law requires to make it (answer yes for an enduring power of attorney)
      `it met the Act's other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it met the Act's other requirements for making it, such as the formal requirements of signing and witnessing (s 44)
      `it is invalid for another reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is invalid for another reason, for example because you were induced to make it by dishonesty or undue influence
GIVETH A `Validity answer`
DECIDE `Can the court declare my power of attorney invalid` IS
    `the s 113 answer` `the attorney` `I made it freely and voluntarily` `I understood its nature and effect` `I had the capacity needed to make another document` `it met the Act's other requirements` `it is invalid for another reason`

@export My attorney acted under a power that was invalid: is the attorney liable to me because of the invalidity?
GIVEN `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of attorney (see the validity question)
      `why the power was invalid` IS AN `Invalidity` @desc Why the power was invalid when used: the document was made in another jurisdiction and does not comply with its requirements; the document had been revoked (wholly or for that power); the power was not exercisable at the time; or it was valid
      `the attorney knew it was invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney knew the power was invalid
      `the attorney knew of the event that made it invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney knew of the event that made it invalid (for example, that you had revoked it)
      `the attorney had reason to believe it was invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney had reason to believe the power was invalid
GIVETH AN `Invalid power answer`
DECIDE `Is my attorney liable for acting under an invalid power` IS
    `the s 98 answer` `the attorney` `why the power was invalid`
        (`knew of the invalidity` `the attorney knew it was invalid` `the attorney knew of the event that made it invalid` `the attorney had reason to believe it was invalid`)

@export My attorney made a transaction with someone under a power that was invalid: is the transaction valid in favour of that person?
GIVEN `why the power was invalid` IS AN `Invalidity` @desc Why the power was invalid when used (see the previous question), or that it was valid
      `the other person knew of the invalidity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who dealt with the attorney knew of the invalidity, knew of the event that caused it, or had reason to believe the power was invalid
GIVETH A `Third person answer`
DECIDE `Is the transaction valid in favour of the other person` IS
    `the s 99(2) answer` `why the power was invalid` `the other person knew of the invalidity`

@export The property my attorney sold under an invalid power has been bought on: is it presumed that the person who dealt with my attorney did not know of the invalidity?
GIVEN `they made a statutory declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who dealt with the attorney made a statutory declaration that they did not know of the invalidity at the time
      `the day of the declaration` IS A DATE @desc The day of that statutory declaration (any date if none)
      `the day the purchase was completed` IS A DATE @desc The day the later purchase (whose purchaser relies on the transaction) was completed
      `the day the transaction was completed` IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction between your attorney and that person was completed
      `the day I made the power of attorney` IS A DATE @desc The day the power of attorney was made
GIVETH A `Purchaser presumption answer`
DECIDE `Is it presumed the other person did not know of the invalidity` IS
    `the s 99(3) answer` `they made a statutory declaration` `the day of the declaration` `the day the purchase was completed` `the day the transaction was completed` `the day I made the power of attorney`

§§ `What my attorney was allowed to do (ss 73, 84, 86-89)`

@export Was my attorney allowed to enter into this transaction, given a possible conflict of interest?
GIVEN `what the transaction could conflict with` IS A `Conflict` @desc What the attorney's duty to you could conflict with in the transaction: the attorney's own interests; the interests of the attorney's relation, business associate or close friend; another duty of the attorney; or nothing
      `where the conflict comes from` IS A `Source of the conflict` @desc Where the conflict comes from: merely that the attorney is related to you; merely that the attorney may inherit from you; merely a dealing with property you and the attorney hold or acquire jointly (or a loan or guarantee for it); the transaction is a gift under s 88; it provides for your dependant under s 89; or something else
      `who authorised it` IS AN `Authorisation` @desc Who authorised it: you, beforehand (this transaction, its type, or conflict transactions generally); the court, beforehand; you, afterwards, while you had capacity; the court, afterwards; or nobody
GIVETH A `Conflict answer`
DECIDE `Was my attorney allowed to enter into this transaction` IS
    `the s 73 answer` `what the transaction could conflict with` `where the conflict comes from` `who authorised it`

@export My attorney entered into a conflict transaction with someone: is it valid in favour of that person?
GIVEN `they knew it was a conflict transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other party to the transaction knew it was a conflict transaction
      `they had reason to believe it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other party had reason to believe it was a conflict transaction
GIVETH AN `Other party answer`
DECIDE `Is the conflict transaction valid in favour of the other party` IS
    `the s 73(9) answer` `they knew it was a conflict transaction` `they had reason to believe it was`

@export Is it presumed that my attorney unduly influenced me into a transaction with them or someone close to them?
GIVEN `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document the attorney acts under (see the validity question)
      `who the transaction was with` IS AN `Other party` @desc Who the transaction was with: the attorney; the attorney's spouse; a blood, marriage, adoptive, de facto, foster or legal-arrangement relative of the attorney; someone the attorney depends on; someone dependent on the attorney; a member of the attorney's household; a business associate of the attorney; a close friend of the attorney (close personal relationship and personal interest in the attorney's welfare); or someone else
GIVETH AN `Undue influence answer`
DECIDE `Is it presumed my attorney unduly influenced me` IS
    `the s 87 answer` `the attorney` `who the transaction was with`

@export Could my attorney under my enduring power of attorney invest my money in this investment?
GIVEN `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document the attorney acts under (see the validity question)
      `a trustee could make it under the Trusts Act 2025` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the investment is one a trustee could make with trust funds under the Trusts Act 2025
      `QCAT approved it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether QCAT (the tribunal) approved the investment
      `I had it when the power became exercisable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you already held the investment when the attorney's power became exercisable (including new shares or options from shares you held)
GIVETH AN `Investment answer`
DECIDE `Could my attorney invest my money this way` IS
    `the s 84 answer` `the attorney` `a trustee could make it under the Trusts Act 2025` `QCAT approved it` `I had it when the power became exercisable`

@export Did my attorney have to keep their own property separate from mine?
GIVEN `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document the attorney acts under (see the validity question)
      `the property is jointly owned by me and the attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the property in question is owned jointly by you and the attorney
      `it was bought jointly to replace jointly owned property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the attorney acquired it jointly in place of property you owned jointly
GIVETH A `Separate property answer`
DECIDE `Did my attorney have to keep their property separate from mine` IS
    `the s 86 answer` `the attorney` `the property is jointly owned by me and the attorney` `it was bought jointly to replace jointly owned property`

@export Could my attorney give away my property or make a donation from it?
GIVEN `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document the attorney acts under (see the validity question)
      `the court or QCAT otherwise authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift was otherwise authorised under the Act, for example by the court under s 118(2)
      `I made gifts like it when I had capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a gift of the kind you made when you had capacity (for example birthday presents to grandchildren, or donations to a charity you supported)
      `I might reasonably be expected to make it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a gift of the kind you might reasonably be expected to make
      `its value is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether its value is no more than is reasonable in all the circumstances, especially your finances (a court or QCAT decides this in a dispute)
GIVETH A `Gift answer`
DECIDE `Could my attorney give away my property` IS
    `the s 88 answer` `the attorney` `the court or QCAT otherwise authorised it` `I made gifts like it when I had capacity` `I might reasonably be expected to make it` `its value is reasonable`

@export Could my attorney pay for someone's needs from my money as my dependant?
GIVEN `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document the attorney acts under (see the validity question)
      `the person depends completely or mainly on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person provided for is completely or mainly dependent on you
      `my enduring power of attorney allows more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your enduring power of attorney expresses an intention that the attorney may provide more than is reasonable
      `the amount is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what was provided is no more than is reasonable in all the circumstances, especially your finances (a court or QCAT decides this in a dispute)
GIVETH A `Dependant answer`
DECIDE `Could my attorney provide for my dependant` IS
    `the s 89 answer` `the attorney` `the person depends completely or mainly on me` `my enduring power of attorney allows more` `the amount is reasonable`

@export Is what my attorney (or the person who got me to sign) did an offence, and what is the most they can be fined?
GIVEN `what they did` IS A `Conduct` @desc What was done: dishonestly getting someone to make or revoke a power of attorney, or an enduring document; the attorney not acting honestly and with reasonable diligence to protect your interests; the attorney using a power they knew was revoked; the attorney using confidential information without authority or reasonable excuse; the attorney not keeping their property separate from yours; or other conduct
GIVETH AN `Offence answer`
DECIDE `What offence has my attorney committed` IS
    IF `the maximum penalty in penalty units` `what they did` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `an offence; the most the court can impose is, in penalty units` (`the maximum penalty in penalty units` `what they did`)
    ELSE `the Act does not settle this: ss 26, 61, 66, 71, 74A and 86 do not make that conduct an offence`

§§ `Compensation from the attorney (ss 66, 106)`

@export Can I get compensation from my attorney, or make them account for their profits, for not complying with the Act?
GIVEN `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document the attorney acts under (see the validity question)
      `the attorney failed to comply with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney failed to comply with the Act when exercising a power (for example, not acting honestly and with reasonable diligence, an unauthorised conflict transaction, a gift the Act does not allow, mixing property)
      `it caused a loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that failure caused a loss to you (or to the principal)
      `the attorney profited from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney made profits as a result of that failure
      `the principal has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal (the person who made the document) has died
GIVETH A `Compensation answer`
DECIDE `Can I get compensation or the profits from my attorney` IS
    `the s 106 answer` `the attorney` `the attorney failed to comply with the Act` `it caused a loss` `the attorney profited from it` `the principal has died`

@export By when must I apply for compensation or an account of profits from the attorney?
GIVEN `the principal has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal (the person who made the document) has died
      `the day the principal died` IS A DATE @desc The day the principal died (any date if alive)
      `the attorney has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney has died
      `the day the attorney died` IS A DATE @desc The day the attorney died (any date if alive)
GIVETH AN `Application time answer`
DECIDE `By when must I apply for compensation from the attorney` IS
    `the s 106 time answer` `the principal has died` `the day the principal died` `the attorney has died` `the day the attorney died`

@export The principal or the attorney has died: is my application for compensation or an account of profits in time?
GIVEN `the principal has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal has died (answer yes or the next question applies)
      `the day the principal died` IS A DATE @desc The day the principal died (any date if alive)
      `the attorney has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney has died
      `the day the attorney died` IS A DATE @desc The day the attorney died (any date if alive)
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you made, or will make, the application to the court or QCAT
GIVETH A MAYBE `Application timing`
DECIDE `Is my compensation application in time` IS
    IF `the principal has died` AND `the attorney has died`
    THEN JUST (`the s 106 timing` (`the earlier of` `the day the principal died` `and` `the day the attorney died`) `the day I apply`)
    ELSE IF `the principal has died`
         THEN JUST (`the s 106 timing` `the day the principal died` `the day I apply`)
         ELSE IF `the attorney has died`
              THEN JUST (`the s 106 timing` `the day the attorney died` `the day I apply`)
              ELSE NOTHING

§§ `A benefit in the estate lost by the attorney's dealing (s 107) -- arises only after the principal has died`

@export I lost my gift or share in the principal's estate because their attorney sold or dealt with the property: can I be compensated out of the estate, and how much?
GIVEN `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document the attorney acted under (see the validity question)
      `my benefit was lost because of the attorney's dealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a benefit you had in the principal's estate (under the will, on intestacy, or by another disposition taking effect on death) was lost because the attorney sold or otherwise dealt with the principal's property
      `who is applying` IS A `Lost benefit applicant` @desc Who is applying: the person whose benefit was lost (even if that person is the attorney); that person's personal representative; or someone else
      `the value of the lost benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of the lost benefit, in Australian dollars
GIVETH A `Lost benefit answer`
DECIDE `Can I apply for compensation for my lost benefit in the estate` IS
    `the s 107 answer` `the attorney` `my benefit was lost because of the attorney's dealing` `who is applying` `the value of the lost benefit`

@export Is my application for compensation for a lost benefit in the principal's estate in time?
GIVEN `the day the principal died` IS A DATE @desc The day the principal died
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you started, or will start, the proceedings in the Supreme Court
GIVETH AN `Application timing`
DECIDE `Is my lost benefit application in time` IS
    `the s 107 timing` `the day the principal died` `the day I apply`

§§ `Property in the will that the attorney dealt with (ss 61A-61D) -- arises only after the principal has died`

@export The attorney sold or mortgaged property left to me in the principal's will: do I take the proceeds instead?
GIVEN `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document the attorney acted under (see the validity question)
      `I am a beneficiary under the will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a beneficiary under the deceased principal's will
      `the attorney dealt with the property under the enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney sold, mortgaged, charged, disposed of or otherwise dealt with the property under the enduring power of attorney
      `the court has made a s 61D order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has made an order under s 61D(1) about it
GIVETH A `Proceeds answer`
DECIDE `Do I take the proceeds of property the attorney dealt with` IS
    `the s 61B answer` `the attorney` `I am a beneficiary under the will` `the attorney dealt with the property under the enduring power of attorney` `the court has made a s 61D order`

@export Can I ask the Supreme Court to confirm or adjust how the proceeds of property the attorney dealt with pass under the will?
GIVEN `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document the attorney acted under (see the validity question)
      `who is applying` IS A `S 61D applicant` @desc Who is applying: a beneficiary under the principal's will; the personal representative of a deceased beneficiary; the principal's personal representative; or someone else
GIVETH A `S 61D answer`
DECIDE `Can I apply to the court about the proceeds` IS
    `the s 61D answer` `the attorney` `who is applying`

@export Is my application to the Supreme Court about the proceeds (s 61D) in time?
GIVEN `the day the principal died` IS A DATE @desc The day the principal died
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you made, or will make, the application
GIVETH AN `Application timing`
DECIDE `Is my application about the proceeds in time` IS
    `the s 61D timing` `the day the principal died` `the day I apply`

@export Can the personal representative distribute the estate without answering to me for it, while my claim about the attorney's dealings is pending?
GIVEN `the day the principal died` IS A DATE @desc The day the principal died
      `the day of the distribution` IS A DATE @desc The day the personal representative distributed (or plans to distribute) the part of the estate
      `the distribution was properly made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the distribution was properly made (a court decides this in a dispute)
      `I agreed in writing or said I would not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, with full legal capacity, told the personal representative in writing that you consent to the distribution or do not intend to apply
      `I gave written notice of my claim before the distribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before the distribution, you gave the personal representative written notice, signed by you or your solicitor, of your application or intended application
      `they had notice my application had started` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the personal representative had written notice that your application had been started in court, or was served with a copy of it, before the distribution
GIVETH A `Distribution answer`
DECIDE `Could the personal representative distribute the estate out of my reach` IS
    `the s 44 answer` `the day the principal died` `the day of the distribution` `the distribution was properly made` `I agreed in writing or said I would not apply` `I gave written notice of my claim before the distribution` `they had notice my application had started`

§§ `Going to court (ss 109A, 110, 122-125)`

@export Can I apply to the Supreme Court about a power of attorney, an advance health directive, or an attorney's exercise of power?
GIVEN `who I am` IS AN `Applicant` @desc Who you are: the principal; their spouse; their child aged 18 or more (including step, adopted or foster); their parent (including step, adoptive, foster or guardian); their sibling aged 18 or more; an attorney; a health provider of the principal; someone else with a sufficient and genuine concern for the principal's rights and interests; or someone else
      `the principal has a spouse, adult child or parent reasonably available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal has a spouse, adult child or parent who is reasonably available (matters only for a sibling)
      `my application is about health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application is about an advance health directive or a power for a health matter (matters only for a health provider)
GIVETH A `Standing answer`
DECIDE `Can I apply to the court about the attorney` IS
    `the s 110 answer` `who I am` `the principal has a spouse, adult child or parent reasonably available` `my application is about health`

@export Which court or tribunal can hear my application about my attorney?
GIVEN `what I am applying for` IS AN `Application kind` @desc What you are applying for: compensation or an account of profits (s 106); compensation for a lost benefit in the estate (s 107); an order about a beneficiary's interest in proceeds (s 61D); records, accounts or an audit (s 122); or another declaration, order, direction or advice about the power or the attorney
      `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document the attorney acts under (see the validity question)
GIVETH A `Forum answer`
DECIDE `Which court or tribunal hears my application` IS
    `the forum answer` `what I am applying for` `the attorney`

@export Can I get the court or QCAT to make my attorney produce accounts, have them audited, or present a management plan?
GIVEN `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document the attorney acts under (see the validity question)
      `the attorney manages my money or property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney is your attorney for a financial matter
      `I am the principal or an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the principal, or someone with a sufficient and genuine concern for the principal's rights and interests
GIVETH A `Records answer`
DECIDE `Can I get my attorney's accounts examined` IS
    `the s 122 answer` `the attorney` `the attorney manages my money or property` `I am the principal or an interested person`

@export Who pays the costs of my Supreme Court application about the attorney?
GIVEN `my application was dismissed as frivolous, vexatious or misconceived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court dismissed your application as frivolous, trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance (s 123)
      `the court made a different order about costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court made its own order about who pays the costs
      `I succeeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you succeeded in the application
GIVETH A `Costs answer`
DECIDE `Who pays the costs` IS
    `the costs answer` `my application was dismissed as frivolous, vexatious or misconceived` `the court made a different order about costs` `I succeeded`

@export By when must the court give me written reasons for its decision?
GIVEN `the day I asked for reasons` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied to the court for written reasons
      `the court considers I have a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court considers you have a sufficient interest in obtaining reasons for its decision
GIVETH A `Reasons answer`
DECIDE `By when must the court give me written reasons` IS
    `the s 124 answer` `the day I asked for reasons` `the court considers I have a sufficient interest`
